 "notes": [
  "tuna_by_origin: tuna (HS 030341-030349, 030487, 160414) that importing countries record as originating in each country, from partners' annual returns to UN Comtrade (all reporters). Importers assign origin by the catching vessel's flag, so this is each flag's fleet landing abroad, not catch in the country's own waters and not a measure of licence fees.",
  "PNA = Parties to the Nauru Agreement: Kiribati, Micronesia (FS), Marshall Islands, Nauru, Palau, Papua New Guinea, Solomon Islands, Tuvalu. The tuna cross-check uses seven of them (not Palau). The applicability screen covers 15 small island states; Marshall Islands is not among them because its partner data are unusable: trade booked to its ship registry swamps the figures.",
  "applicability: exp_cov_12m / imp_cov_12m = share of the country's trade (excluding ships and aircraft) with partners whose latest monthly Comtrade data are within 12 months (6m variants alongside). exp_ratio / imp_ratio = partner-reported total ÷ the country's own total, both excluding HS 88-89, for the latest year both exist (ratio_year). own_source says whether the own total is the annual return or monthly returns scaled to 12.",
  "exp/imp_mirror_usd_m and exp/imp_own_usd_m exclude ships and aircraft; the HS 88-89 amounts taken out are in *_ships_aircraft_usd_m. In the source CSV the column named 'mirror_excl_88_89_usd_m' holds that excluded amount, not a total.",
  "Kiribati's export ratio (6.6×) is the largest among peers with their own data, against 1.4-2.1× for Papua New Guinea, Maldives and Comoros. Ships and aircraft removal lowers Maldives' export ratio from 2.65 to 1.62. Marshall Islands: partner data unusable (ship registry).",
  "Import coverage is weaker everywhere (about 40-85 percent of trade with prompt reporters); partner data are a usable export record for the tuna exporters (95 percent or more with prompt reporters).",
  "Ratios are read annually only; the Kiribati 2024 import ratio (0.04) is dominated by one outsized line in Kiribati's January 2024 return and should not be quoted (see national_accounts.json)."
 ]
}